et the downloader for this IE.\"\"\"\n    self._downloader = downloader\n```\n\nI think that's it. OK.\n\nActually, to be safe against `to_screen` being called with args, I'll give the fake downloader flexible methods with *args/**kwargs.\n\nNow, `_sort_formats` \u2014 check if it needs downloader. Let me fetch.\n\nLet me also consider: does `_real_extract` get called directly, or should I call `ie.extract(url)`? `extract()` does initialization stuff (sets _ready, calls _real_initialize, etc.). Calling `_real_extract` directly is simpler and focuses coverage on lines 42-101. I'll call `_real_extract` directly.\n\nNow let me also double-check `determine_ext`:\n\n```python\ndef determine_ext(url, default_ext=u'unknown_video'):\n    guess = url.partition(u'?')[0].rpartition(u'.')[2]\n    if re.match(r'^[0-9a-zA-Z]{1,4}$', guess):\n        return guess\n    return default_ext\n```\n\nHmm, actually I think it's:\n\n```python\ndef determine_ext(url, default_ext=u'unknown_video'):\n    guess = url.partition(u'?')[0].rpartition(u'.')[2]\n    if re.match(r'^[0-9a-zA-Z]{1,4}$', guess):\n        return guess\n    return default_ext\n```\n\nWait, but for 'https://cdn.example.com/hls/300040/master.m3u8' -> guess = 'm3u8' -> matches -> 'm3u8'. Good. For '.f4m' -> 'f4m'. For '.mp4' -> 'mp4'. Good.\n\nHmm, actually the real determine_ext in youtube-dl:\n\n```python\ndef determine_ext(url, default_ext=u'unknown_video'):\n    if url == u'':\n        return default_ext\n    guess = url.partition(u'?')[0].rpartition(u'.')[2]\n    if re.match(r'^[0-9a-zA-Z]{1,4}$', guess):\n        return guess\n    return default_ext\n```\n\nSomething like that. Fine.\n\nNow, the m3u8 format returned by my mocked `_extract_m3u8_formats` \u2014 after `_sort_formats` runs, the formats get sorted. The sort key involves quality fields. My fake formats should be sortable. Let me make them simple dicts with 'url', 'format_id', 'ext', maybe 'height'/'tbr'. The sort function in youtube-dl:\n\n```python\ndef _s